{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRyCP4ZXq9U3W7u5UGuT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A68so2vrroS4saCieVcfae","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\", s.index(\"def build_system\"))]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two blocks, each with its own breakpoint. The static instructions come first so a change in the\n    # athlete context (a new fact from save_fact, a new day) only invalidates the second block.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n'''\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Caching fix\n\n**Cause:** `build_system` joined the static `INSTRUCTIONS` and the per-athlete context (which includes the\nfacts list) into one text block with a single `cache_control` breakpoint. Caching is prefix-based, so any\nchange to the facts changed the whole block and the next call re-created the cache (`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`).\n\n**Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`):** the system prompt is now two blocks, each with its own breakpoint:\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS` (static)\n2. `athlete_context(...)` (today, zones, goal, facts, language)\n\nA `save_fact` now only invalidates block 2. Tool filtering is unchanged.\n\n**Caveats (not verified; I had no API access to test):**\n- The minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet 4.5 is 1024 tokens. Judging by the logs (~1046 total, including\n  tools and ~100 tokens of context), the static part alone is probably around 800-900 tokens. If so, block 1\n  will not be cached on its own and the fix won't show a benefit until the static prefix is over 1024 tokens\n  (for example, a longer instruction set). Check `cache_creation_input_tokens` right after a `save_fact` in\n  `logs/usage.jsonl`: it should drop to the context size, not ~1000.\n- `tools` come before `system` in the cache prefix, so a message that selects a different tool group also\n  misses the cache. That predates this change and I left the keyword filtering alone, as NOTES.md asks.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":673,"cache_read_input_tokens":24665,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":673},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70cfa930-10d7-4a09-8982-c8e6fca56d16","uuid":"52256991-d5b2-4a77-ac33-67889d56b594","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:41:16.118Z","request_id":"req_011CgRyCNoSgTDLqP5wuttD7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01A68so2vrroS4saCieVcfae":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-BQuLdp && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('bot.py').read()\nold=s[s.index(\"def build_system\"):s.index(\"# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\", s.index(\"def build_system\"))]\nnew='''def build_system(a, today):\n    # Two blocks, each with its own breakpoint. The static instructions come first so a change in the\n    # athlete context (a new fact from save_fact, a new day) only invalidates the second block.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS, \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n\n'''\nopen('bot.py','w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Caching fix\n\n**Cause:** `build_system` joined the static `INSTRUCTIONS` and the per-athlete context (which includes the\nfacts list) into one text block with a single `cache_control` breakpoint. Caching is prefix-based, so any\nchange to the facts changed the whole block and the next call re-created the cache (`cache_read_input_tokens: 0`).\n\n**Change (`bot.py`, `build_system`):** the system prompt is now two blocks, each with its own breakpoint:\n1. `INSTRUCTIONS` (static)\n2. `athlete_context(...)` (today, zones, goal, facts, language)\n\nA `save_fact` now only invalidates block 2. Tool filtering is unchanged.\n\n**Caveats (not verified; I had no API access to test):**\n- The minimum cacheable prefix on Sonnet 4.5 is 1024 tokens. Judging by the logs (~1046 total, including\n  tools and ~100 tokens of context), the static part alone is probably around 800-900 tokens. If so, block 1\n  will not be cached on its own and the fix won't show a benefit until the static prefix is over 1024 tokens\n  (for example, a longer instruction set). Check `cache_creation_input_tokens` right after a `save_fact` in\n  `logs/usage.jsonl`: it should drop to the context size, not ~1000.\n- `tools` come before `system` in the cache prefix, so a message that selects a different tool group also\n  misses the cache. That predates this change and I left the keyword filtering alone, as NOTES.md asks.\nE"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01A68so2vrroS4saCieVcfae":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-BQuLdp"}}}
